 "about_text": "Base Gallery is a contemporary art gallery founded in 1986 in Tokyo, originally established as Matrix Japan S.A. It opened its first exhibition space in Ginza in 1988, moved to Kyobashi in 1995, and has been based in Kayabacho, in Tokyo's financial district, since 2004. The gallery mounts six to eight curated exhibitions a year and also runs an international art-dealing business spanning Japan, the Americas, Europe and Asia, handling modern and contemporary painting, sculpture and photography. It is particularly known for contemporary art from Southeast and East Asia. The gallery has also produced projects exploring the crossover of art and music, including the museum artegio in Yufuin, and operates a second space, Base Gallery Hakata, in Fukuoka.",
